Phasmid: font fallback (Windows profiles)

What:     A windows profile falls back per character as Windows Chrome does:
          the standard style from weight 700, then Windows' emoji, Unicode
          block and script tables (Han by content locale, then system
          locale), then its wide-coverage lists, and only then fontconfig's
          sort over the claimed font set. Families are asked for by name, so
          the browser's name gate decides which exist. Courier, MS Sans
          Serif, MS Serif and Times map to their TrueType families as on
          Windows. Linux profiles are unchanged.
Why:      Emoji and CJK fallback picked Linux fonts (Noto Color Emoji,
          fontconfig's CJK face) under a Windows UA.
Profile:  os.family; the Han locale follows locale.languages
Hooks:    third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/linux/font_cache_linux.cc
          FontCache::PlatformFallbackFontForCharacter; new
          fonts/linux/windows_fallback.{h,cc} (a copy of
          win/font_fallback_win.cc); fonts/font_cache.cc GetFontData,
          IsPlatformFamilyMatchAvailable; platform BUILD.gn
Contexts: main, same- and cross-origin iframe, worker, shared worker, service
          worker, OffscreenCanvas in workers; headless and headful.
Guard:    tests/guards/fonts/windows_metrics.py

